    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.estrada_index - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.estrada_index.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.estrada_index()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate the Estrada index of the graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.estrada_index()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate the Estrada index of the graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.estrada_index()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Calculate the Estrada index of the graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCalculate the Estrada index of the graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L86121-L86215){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.estrada_index()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Estrada index](../assets/graphs/estrada-index.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A five-node graph and a card that exponentiates each of its five adjacency eigenvalues, from e to the 2.641 (14.03) down to e to the -1.776 (0.17), and adds them to the Estrada index 17.18.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe Estrada index is the sum of exponentials of the eigenvalues of the adjacency matrix:\n\n`EE(G) = Σᵢ exp(λᵢ)`\n\nwhere `λᵢ` are the eigenvalues of the adjacency matrix. This index captures the degree of\nfolding or compactness of a network, and is related to subgraph centrality and the number of\nclosed walks.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The Estrada index. Returns 0.0 for empty graphs, 1.0 for single-node graphs.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is directed (Estrada index is only defined for undirected graphs).\n:::\n\n## Technical Notes {.doc-technical-notes}\n\nThe Estrada index $EE(G) = \\sum_i e^{\\lambda_i} = \\mathrm{tr}(e^A)$ (Estrada, 2000)\nis the trace of the matrix exponential of the adjacency matrix, and Taylor-expanding\n$e^A$ shows that it counts closed walks of every length weighted by $1/k!$: so it\ngrows whenever a graph carries more short closed walks (triangles, tetrahedra, and\nhigher cliques). Because $EE = n$ for the edgeless graph and increases with every\nadditional walk, it always satisfies $EE(G) \\ge n$. It is tightly connected to the\n*subgraph centrality*: node $i$'s score\n$SC(i) = \\sum_j \\phi_j(i)^2 e^{\\lambda_j}$ is the $i$-th diagonal entry of $e^A$,\nso $EE = \\sum_i SC(i)$. Computation costs $O(n^3)$ via dense eigendecomposition of\n$A$; only undirected inputs are supported since the definition assumes a real\nsymmetric spectrum.\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~subgraph_centrality`) \n\n:   Each node's share of the index.\n\n[](`~adjacency_spectrum`) \n\n:   The eigenvalues the index is built from.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nA single edge has eigenvalues `1` and `-1`, so its Estrada index is\n`exp(1) + exp(-1)`; with no edges, every eigenvalue is `0` and the index is the number of\nnodes:\n\n::: {#24b95ef6 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nedge = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\")])\nempty = ec.Graph().add_nodes([\"A\", \"B\"])\n\nround(edge.estrada_index(), 3), empty.estrada_index()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n(3.086, 2.0)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Folded molecules\n\n`molecules()` holds the graphs of seven small molecules, one node per atom (leaving out\nthe hydrogens) and one edge per bond. Estrada introduced the index in 2000 to measure how\nfolded a protein chain is, and a compact molecule scores higher than a long one with the\nsame atoms: the branched isobutane higher than the chain of butane:\n\n::: {#a6ee9c32 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmolecules = ec.molecules()\n\n[\n    (name, round(molecules[name].estrada_index(), 3))\n    for name in [\"butane\", \"isobutane\"]\n]\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n[('butane', 7.636), ('isobutane', 7.829)]\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nThe index is the sum of the subgraph centralities of the atoms. In caffeine, the atoms\nof the two rings, which close the most short walks, add the most, and the three carbons\nand two oxygens hanging off the rings the least:\n\n::: {#06a64d84 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncaffeine = molecules[\"caffeine\"].subgraph_centrality()\ncentrality = caffeine.get_node_attrs(\"subgraph_centrality\")\n\nround(sum(centrality.values()), 3), round(caffeine.estrada_index(), 3)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(35.111, 35.111)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#242afee1 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ncaffeine.plot(\n    color_by=\"subgraph_centrality\", color_scale=\"sequential\",\n    label_by=\"label\", seed=1,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-975840b8:#86b6ef;--ect-e96c6d08:#174075;--ect-f572b836:#4f7bb3;--ect-6425850a:#0d366b;--ect-e28c6970:#194278;--ect-e58b2c1a:#113a6f;--ect-f8094ac6:#79a8e1;--ect-472663e1:#6d9bd3;--ect-6826a5f9:#608ec6;--ect-9d43aea2:#5480b8;--ect-5ee57d66:#4874ab;--ect-3c980f0e:#3c679e;--ect-ec386ef0:#305a91;--ect-97f76ec5:#254e84;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-6970a796:#5d7fa7;--ect-114896fe:#102c51;--ect-a5899a45:#37567d;--ect-bf50105f:#09254a;--ect-cc719475:#112e54;--ect-abcb2494:#0b284d;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-975840b8:#184f95;--ect-e96c6d08:#bed6f3;--ect-f572b836:#678ec2;--ect-6425850a:#cde2fb;--ect-e28c6970:#bad3f1;--ect-e58b2c1a:#c7ddf8;--ect-f8094ac6:#2c5d9f;--ect-472663e1:#3d6caa;--ect-6826a5f9:#4f7ab4;--ect-9d43aea2:#6089be;--ect-5ee57d66:#7297c9;--ect-3c980f0e:#84a6d3;--ect-ec386ef0:#96b5dd;--ect-97f76ec5:#a8c4e7;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-6970a796:#103768;--ect-114896fe:#8595aa;--ect-a5899a45:#486387;--ect-bf50105f:#8f9eaf;--ect-cc719475:#8293a8;--ect-abcb2494:#8b9aad;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-975840b8:#86b6ef;--ect-e96c6d08:#174075;--ect-f572b836:#4f7bb3;--ect-6425850a:#0d366b;--ect-e28c6970:#194278;--ect-e